      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "These data are consistent with an analysis of CMB dipole signals taken from the Wilkinson Microwave Anisotropy Probe",
          "added": "2026-08-11"
        },
        {
          "text": "A universe born from a rotating black hole should inherit its axis of rotation as a preferred axis",
          "added": "2026-08-11"
        },
        {
          "text": "the total momentum and angular momentum of the matter in the universe are zero",
          "added": "2026-08-11"
        },
        {
          "text": "most galaxies should therefore tend to rotate in a preferred direction",
          "added": "2026-08-11"
        },
        {
          "text": "The mean values of the right ascension and declination of the preferred axis are therefore",
          "added": "2026-08-11"
        },
        {
          "text": "showed a large-scale bulk flow of galaxy clusters with speed 630 km/s",
          "added": "2026-08-11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Applying the law of cosines to this triangle gives",
          "added": "2026-08-11"
        },
        {
          "text": "The cosmological constant generated by the rotation of the universe would not be constant",
          "added": "2026-08-11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Because the angular momentum of the universe is conserved, the angular velocity of the universe decreases as the universe expands",
          "added": "2026-08-11"
        }
      ]
